Seeded defect for tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/DynamicDifferentialTests.cs

Reverts the #213 part of 70eb3c3 (#232) that still applies: BTreeIndex.FindChildIndex descends
to the right of a separator equal to the key again, also when the caller asks for the leftmost
leaf. In a non-unique index, which is what every DynamicCollection index is (its keys carry no
document id, #234), copies of a key left of an equal separator are then skipped by a forward
range scan. The rest of 70eb3c3 (splits by size, #217; Delete searching every child that can
hold the key) stays.

With it applied, 96 rows fail on upstream 0450b97 that are not candidates (tools/oracle-seeds.cs:
CAUGHT, 96 new failures), all on the indexed ways (indexed/api and indexed/blql, against both
oracles): every equality and range on an indexed field with ties that straddle a leaf split, e.g.
  indexed/api linq: count == 5: expected 70 documents, got 51
      ran as: QueryIndexAsync("idx_count", 5, 5, ascending: true) with the filter as residual
  indexed/blql linq: when == t5: expected 78 documents, got 43
  indexed/api linq: nick == null: expected 108 documents, got 44 (the null bucket too)
The typed collection is not affected: its keys are unique, so no separator equals a search key.

Reproduce: git apply tests/BLite.Tests/Oracles/Seeds/DynamicDifferentialTests.revert-70eb3c3-leftmost-descent.patch && dotnet test tests/BLite.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~DynamicDifferentialTests
Restore:   git checkout -- src

